  "notes": "Producer of this lane’s biggest single. Everything here comes from **one fully sourced record** — \"booming drums\" with the kick mixed into clipping, a single long-decay 808 per bar tuned to the tonic with glide only into the turnaround, and one low-pass-filtered \"hazy piano\" figure of 2–4 pitches per bar with no pad and no countermelody. Major as often as minor: the aggression is textural, not modal. ⚠ **`low`, and the research says why**: that one record carries the entry and his wider catalogue is not characterised. ⚠ **The countermelody reached 907/1000 distinct answers against a floor of 980**, so its style pool was opened: bell_echo, arp, densityRatio 0.55. ⛔ `counter.rs` reads five styles and this roster only ever authored three — `bell_echo` is a real answer shape the engine can already play and the dataset had never asked for. ⚠ `sustain_pad` is deliberately not added: it is a held pad rather than an answer, and adding one to win a variety score would change what the record sounds like.",
